[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_ubd4d")
dialogue_id = "debate_small_industries"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Small Industries"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: I have read that in the Old World, one could buy a robe for the price of two rice balls.
historian: To achieve such efficiency, these robes were made in great big halls by hundreds of tailors all working off the same pattern.
historian: They in turn received cloth from a thousand weavers across a dozen provinces.
historian: And the products were distributed all over the world.
historian: Today, a robe is made by a chain of artisans, each trusting in the other's skill.
historian: It is an expensive item that few of us can buy on a whim.
historian: It seems obvious to prefer a cheaper price, but it comes at a cost to us as a society.
historian: Would you rather be one of those hundreds of tailors, making the same robe for people you will never meet, or today's artisan, making a robe that your village priest will wear?
historian: A unified world is efficient, but in it we become identical shingles in a giant roof, unable to see how our efforts impact the world around us."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
